---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../data/site';

/**
 * This policy describes what the site as built actually does. It is accurate
 * for the current implementation: no analytics, no cookies, no third-party
 * embeds and no tracking. If any of those are added later, this page has to be
 * updated in the same change — see PRIVACY-1 in the verification checklist.
 */
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Yala Energy Limited handles personal information submitted through this website."
  path="/privacy/"
  lede="How Yala Energy Limited handles the personal information you give us through this website. Written to describe what this site actually does, not what a template assumes it does."
  updated="27 October 2026"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Yala Energy Limited is a private company limited by shares, incorporated in Zambia. For any
      question about this policy or about information we hold, email
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      A named data-protection contact and the company's registered address for data-protection
      correspondence are to be confirmed before launch.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What this website collects</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not use analytics, advertising, behavioural tracking or third-party
      embeds, and it sets no cookies of its own. There is no visitor profiling.
    </p>
    <p>
      The only personal information this site collects is what you type into an enquiry form and
      submit:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name and the company or organisation you represent.</li>
      <li>Your business email address.</li>
      <li>Your country and, on the engineering form, your project's location.</li>
      <li>Project details you choose to provide: capacity, stage, service required, whether storage is in scope, and timeline.</li>
      <li>The content of your message.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each form also carries two anti-spam fields: a hidden field that genuine visitors never fill
      in, and the time the form was rendered in your browser. Neither identifies you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Browser storage</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not write cookies, <code>localStorage</code> or any other persistent browser
      storage. Nothing about your visit is kept on your device between sessions by us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why we use it, and on what basis</h2>
    <p>
      We use what you send solely to read, assess and respond to your enquiry, and to carry on the
      conversation that follows from it. The lawful basis is our legitimate interest in responding
      to a business enquiry that you initiated, and taking steps at your request before entering
      into any agreement.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not use enquiry details for marketing, we do not add you to a mailing list, and we do
      not sell, rent or trade personal information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p>Enquiry content is seen by:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Yala Energy personnel handling the relevant enquiry route.</li>
      <li>Our email and form-handling providers, strictly as processors of the message in transit and at rest.</li>
      <li>Professional advisers, where an enquiry needs legal, technical or financial input — and only to the extent needed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Our providers may process and store data outside Zambia. The specific providers in use, and
      the safeguards that apply to any transfer, are to be confirmed and listed here before launch.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiries that do not lead to a business relationship are deleted within 24 months. Where an
      enquiry leads to a commercial relationship, correspondence is kept for as long as that
      relationship lasts, plus the period required by Zambian company and tax law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us for a copy of the information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, ask us
      to delete it, or object to our using it. Email
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a> and we will respond within 30 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are not satisfied with how we have handled your information, you may complain to the
      relevant data-protection authority. Under Zambia's Data Protection Act, that is the Data
      Protection Commissioner.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      This site is served over HTTPS. Form submissions are transmitted over an encrypted
      connection, and no credential, API key or secret is present in anything delivered to your
      browser.
    </p>
    <p>
      No web form is the right channel for confidential or commercially sensitive material, and
      every form on this site says so. Please email us and we will agree a secure route.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Demo mode</h2>
    <p>
      If this deployment has no submission endpoint configured, the forms run in a clearly labelled
      demo mode: your entries are validated in your own browser and then discarded. Nothing is
      transmitted and nothing is stored. The form tells you so on screen rather than implying a
      message was delivered.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the revised version is published here with a new "last updated" date.
      Any change that materially affects how we use information already given to us will be
      notified directly to the people affected.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
